<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- The California Supreme Court opening brief on the merits' Word styles; fb render builds docx/reference.docx from
     pandoc's default reference with them (tools/fb/src/docxref.rs), matching typst/cal-opening-brief-on-the-merits.typ:
     TeX Gyre Schola 13 pt everywhere (the typst face, vendored in fonts/; footnotes included, rule 8.204(b)(4)); body
     lines exact at 413 twips (20.65 pt, the typst body pitch: 1.5 spaced or more, rule 8.204(b)(5)), first-line indent
     0.5 in; headings, block quotations, footnotes and the tables single spaced (line 271 auto: LibreOffice sets a
     single line of TeX Gyre Schola 0.94 em, closer than solid; 1.13 times that is 13.77 pt, the typst single pitch); headings bold, black (level 1 centered
     capitals; numbered levels with the label in a 0.5 in box and the title hanging after it); US Letter, 1.5 in left
     and right, 1 in bottom (rule 8.204(b)(6)). The top margin and the footers are in the section docx/cal.lua writes
     (FORMBOOK_FINAL): 1.1 in top, since TeX Gyre Schola's ascent sets the first line of a page above a 1 in margin in
     LibreOffice (typst sets it on the margin); page numbers from the cover on, none shown on the cover (titlePg,
     rule 8.204(b)(7)); footnotes numbered through the brief. -->
<reference xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" styles="merge" theme-font="TeX Gyre Schola" strip-theme-fonts="true">
